Add E-UTRA band 31 (450 MHz) to the ns-3 LTE module.

3GPP TS 36.101: downlink 462.5-467.5 MHz (NDL 9870-9919), uplink 452.5-457.5 MHz
(NUL 27210-27259). Row fields: band, FDL_low, NOffs-DL, NDL range, FUL_low,
NOffs-UL, NUL range.

Two changes:
  1. the band 31 row in the EARFCN table;
  2. GetCarrierFrequency classified every EARFCN >= 7000 as uplink, which only
     holds up to band 21. FDD downlink EARFCNs span 0-17999 in TS 36.101, so the
     downlink branch is taken below 18000.

Tested against ns-3.48.

--- a/src/lte/model/lte-spectrum-value-helper.cc
+++ b/src/lte/model/lte-spectrum-value-helper.cc
@@ -89,6 +89,7 @@
     {19, 875, 6000, 6000, 6149, 830, 24000, 24000, 24149},
     {20, 791, 6150, 6150, 6449, 832, 24150, 24150, 24449},
     {21, 1495.9, 6450, 6450, 6599, 1447.9, 24450, 24450, 24599},
+    {31, 462.5, 9870, 9870, 9919, 452.5, 27210, 27210, 27259},
     {33, 1900, 36000, 36000, 36199, 1900, 36000, 36000, 36199},
     {34, 2010, 36200, 36200, 36349, 2010, 36200, 36200, 36349},
     {35, 1850, 36350, 36350, 36949, 1850, 36350, 36350, 36949},
@@ -106,7 +107,7 @@
 LteSpectrumValueHelper::GetCarrierFrequency(uint32_t earfcn)
 {
     NS_LOG_FUNCTION(earfcn);
-    if (earfcn < 7000)
+    if (earfcn < 18000)
     {
         // FDD downlink
         return GetDownlinkCarrierFrequency(earfcn);
